---
import { EMAIL, LINKEDIN_URL, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
	title={`About · ${SITE_TITLE}`}
	description="Background, how I work and how to reach me. Product manager at Front Payment in Stavanger, previously at SELISE Digital Platforms."
>
	<article class="container page-top">
		<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
		<h1>Nafees Faraz</h1>
		<p class="lede">
			I'm a product manager in Stavanger, working on payment and onboarding platforms at Front Payment.
		</p>

		<h2>How I got here</h2>
		<p>
			I studied business administration at BRAC University in Dhaka. In 2015 I joined SELISE Digital
			Platforms, which builds digital products for companies across Europe. I started as a product owner
			and became a senior product owner in 2019.
		</p>
		<p>
			Over six years at SELISE I worked on ecommerce, portals and internal platforms for brands such as
			Läderach, Vorwerk, SWICA and Generali. I delivered more than 50 digital solutions that contribute
			about 3.5 million CHF in annual recurring revenue, and I hired and mentored more than five product
			managers and analysts.
		</p>
		<p>
			In 2021 I moved to Norway for an MSc in Business Administration at the University of Stavanger,
			specialising in business development and innovation. In March 2022 I joined Front Payment.
		</p>
		<p>
			At Front Payment I own FrontGO, our payments platform, which now serves 160+ active clients. I've
			launched embedded payment and ecommerce products that bring in about 2 MNOK a year in recurring
			revenue across the portfolio, and delivered live integrations with Worldline, Nets, BankID,
			Experian, Tripletex and PowerOffice Go, among others. In 2026 I built <a href="/work/onboardr/"
				>OnboardR</a
			>, our merchant-onboarding portal, end to end with Claude Code.
		</p>

		<h2>How I work</h2>
		<p>
			I start with the system around a product: who touches it, which checks it has to pass, what it
			connects to and what happens when a step fails. Then I cut the first version down to the job it has
			to do well.
		</p>
		<p>
			I write things down: decisions, open questions and a running log of what's done. The work then
			survives handovers, and nobody has to rediscover what the team already knew.
		</p>
		<p>
			And I work AI-first. On OnboardR that meant holding every role at once, with Claude Code carrying
			much of the implementation and me accountable for what shipped.
		</p>

		<h2>Details</h2>
		<dl class="details">
			<div>
				<dt>Based in</dt>
				<dd>Stavanger, Norway</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>Languages</dt>
				<dd>English and Bengali. I'm learning Norwegian.</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>Education</dt>
				<dd>
					MSc in Business Administration, University of Stavanger (2021–2023)<br />
					BBA, BRAC University (2013–2016)
				</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>Certification</dt>
				<dd>Certified Scrum Master, Scrum Alliance (2024)</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>Tools</dt>
				<dd>Claude Code, Git and GitHub Actions, Figma, Jira, Confluence, Postman, Azure DevOps</dd>
			</div>
		</dl>

		<h2 id="contact">Get in touch</h2>
		<p>
			Email is the best way to reach me: <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>. I'm also on <a
				href={LINKEDIN_URL}>LinkedIn</a
			>.
		</p>
	</article>
</Base>

<style>
	h1 {
		margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
	}
	h2 {
		margin: 3rem 0 1rem;
	}
	.details {
		margin: 0;
	}
	.details div {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.15rem 1.5rem;
		padding: 0.9rem 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
	}
	.details div:last-child {
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
	}
	dt {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.8125rem;
		color: var(--fg-subtle);
	}
	dd {
		margin: 0;
	}
	@media (min-width: 40rem) {
		.details div {
			grid-template-columns: 9rem minmax(0, 1fr);
			align-items: baseline;
		}
	}
</style>
